course: dictionary
lesson: 9607
title: Stringy and tough words
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words paint a picture with a feeling of touch. Stringy means made of thin, tough strands, like pieces of string. «When you cut yourself, platelets and stringy fibres make a net that plugs the cut and hardens into a scab.» The clues are net, plugs and hardens: the fibres are long and thin, joined together like strings.
explain: Stringy can describe more than one thing, so check the words around it. Swap in your meaning: "made of thin strings" fits the sentence, so it is right. The same word can mean tough food, thin hair or a thin person, so always look at what is being described.
fact: Stringy means full of thin, tough strands, like strings.
fact: «Stringy» can describe food that is hard to chew, such as «stringy celery» or «stringy meat».
fact: «Stringy» can describe hair that is thin and hangs in long, straight strands.
fact: In the body, «stringy fibres» help make a net that plugs a cut, and that is how a scab forms.
fact: The word changes its form: stringy, stringier, stringiest.
exercise: «When you cut yourself, platelets and stringy fibres make a net that plugs the cut.» What does stringy mean here? | Wet and sticky like jam | Shiny and smooth | *Made of thin, tough strands | Very loud
exercise: Mum says the celery is stringy. What does she mean? | *It has tough fibres that are hard to chew | It is cold and crisp | Its colour is wrong | It tastes of sugar
exercise: «Her stringy hair hung in long, straight strands.» What does stringy mean here? | Curly and bouncy | Coloured bright blue | *Thin and hanging in long strands | Very short and neat
test: «The cheese stretched into long, stringy strings when Ben pulled the pizza slice apart.» What does stringy mean here? | Burnt and black | Cold and hard | *Stretching into thin strings | Sweet and sticky
test: «The stringy runner was thin, with lean, wiry muscles.» What does stringy mean here? | Hairy and bald | Fat and round | *Thin, with lean, wiry muscles | Tall and loud
exam: Which sentence uses stringy correctly? | Her laugh was stringy | The sky was stringy and blue | *The beans were stringy, so they were tough to chew | The lamp was stringy and warm
